{2}}=49.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186531588 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064358 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7de4234d-932f-537c-9eae-746e1711cccd" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing a Positive Number by a Negative Number"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15c6634c-de5b-5ef4-94a5-e6507f1042b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530904} {:answer/id #uuid "57aebd5e-28ee-528f-94d6-0490b58ea004" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531057} {:answer/id #uuid "6c71de70-51c8-5f75-b420-bfb08a683bd3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531107} {:answer/id #uuid "778ca7f1-f188-5a4c-9f4d-93061d1d1614" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531130} {:answer/id #uuid "e8807038-60fd-56bb-b1ea-3ea4788dbb98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531332}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "15c6634c-de5b-5ef4-94a5-e6507f1042b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530904} :answer-field/id #uuid "9e22da01-1a4a-5c86-bce5-b7f59218a6c7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531495}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "43993959-de6b-5c51-8ec3-a8748bbd2836" :question/math-academy-id "q-42849" :question/problem "$240÷(-12)=$" :question/worked-solution "We have to divide a positive number $(240)$ by a negative one $(-12).$ So the result will be negative:\n\n$$\n240÷(-12)=-\\boxed{}\n$$\n\nNow, to compute the number that goes in the box, we divide $240$ by $12$ without any signs: $240÷12=20.$ Therefore,  we get\n\n$$\n240÷(-12)=-20.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106387 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105756 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "61c58110-9813-5588-81d2-5735718589aa" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Adjacent Vertices and Sides"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c419b61-5a46-5473-9f9c-69d6583578ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\overset{―}{BC}$ and $\\overset{―}{CD}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530919} {:answer/id #uuid "5d42bed0-f63c-52f9-aaba-24bbc5307a2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\overset{―}{EF}$ and $\\overset{―}{AF}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531069} {:answer/id #uuid "87466857-7a97-567a-a500-0444bea69135" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\overset{―}{AF}$ and $\\overset{―}{BC}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531158} {:answer/id #uuid "a0a523df-39f6-5455-a248-9f96091e4381" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\overset{―}{CD}$ and $\\overset{―}{EF}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531211} {:answer/id #uuid "efc05c08-8179-58c3-998e-c6722d526194" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{―}{AB}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531350}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a0a523df-39f6-5455-a248-9f96091e4381" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\overset{―}{CD}$ and $\\overset{―}{EF}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531211} :answer-field/id #uuid "4c12aef7-11e0-5997-a6ca-e0ed6be72cc9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186104470}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2e704e4c-eb76-5811-9abf-e7757267964c" :question/math-academy-id "q-52827" :question/problem "![](images/14/14b60e420cd071378f0b6a6f4c23891779733ae648d667f910617da9341aa9e4.png)\n\nWhich sides are consecutive to $\\overset{―}{DE}?$" :question/worked-solution "Two sides are consecutive if they have a vertex in common. Therefore, $\\overset{―}{CD}$ and $\\overset{―}{EF}$ are consecutive sides to $\\overset{―}{DE}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186434587 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073880 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7435b531-e922-5db5-8140-463b7e66dd64" :knowledge-point/title "Completing a Statement by Interpreting a Fraction as a Ratio"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "054493ad-1415-5db0-b84c-4d536af78614" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$7$ and $2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434514} {:answer/id #uuid "1a035a2a-633d-5a5c-b420-249e8d7c1027" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$7$ and $5$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434519} {:answer/id #uuid "5769e886-78e0-5555-b151-65573a3aec35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$5$ and $7$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434531} {:answer/id #uuid "5e038896-7d0b-533b-86ab-5c8b1e2e7441" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2$ and $7$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434532} {:answer/id #uuid "e3ac12d5-57ed-5086-bb29-ed2ffc3f46c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2$ and $9$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434557}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5e038896-7d0b-533b-86ab-5c8b1e2e7441" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2$ and $7$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434532} :answer-field/id #uuid "f2be6992-76df-55a5-9229-cf46bc57da05" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434575}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f0557329-924c-5116-b187-33f66bcdf532" :question/math-academy-id "q-60249" :question/problem "From left to right, what are the missing numbers in the following sentence?\n\nIn a beverage, there are $\\frac{2}{7}$ teaspoons of ginger for each teaspoon of sugar. Therefore, the beverage has a ratio of $\\boxed{}$ teaspoons of ginger to $\\boxed{}$ teaspoons of sugar." :question/worked-solution "Let's rewrite the fraction $\\frac{2}{7}$ as a ratio:\n\n$$\n2:7\n$$\n\nTherefore, the beverage has a ratio of $2$ teaspoons of ginger to $7$ teaspoons of sugar."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186531593 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073900 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "83bbdad9-c2a5-5caa-a4e9-2a0c904c605b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Distance Between Two Points: Crossing the Axis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07de2851-2484-55be-a23c-13409d875b06" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530875} {:answer/id #uuid "bffc5c5f-557f-50da-ae87-c04af13e2bd7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531269} {:answer/id #uuid "c7bc695b-36dc-5765-94b9-c570c3a39720" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531279} {:answer/id #uuid "f8f314d3-fb52-56ee-b641-75480fce47ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531371} {:answer/id #uuid "fac4f137-1d76-5d07-8f85-2cdd7cfafb4d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531373}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bffc5c5f-557f-50da-ae87-c04af13e2bd7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531269} :answer-field/id #uuid "b85440a4-40ff-52cb-af1f-cc98ab1fcd3d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531509}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "553e8be5-17eb-5fb4-be35-fa84cdea996b" :question/math-academy-id "q-60651" :question/problem "![](images/c9/c9b42a179625b667cb54f1b597127809d851a1b7a830a2632b09402ecb790330.png)\n\nWhat is the distance between the points $(3,2)$  and $(-2,2)?$" :question/worked-solution "**Method 1** \n\nThe distance between two points is the length of the line segment that connects them.\n\nFrom the diagram, we see that the length of the segment is $5$ units, so the distance equals $5.$\n\n![](images/49/498674b4a4667b57be1574a081bbb948350754ed8993c14428ad8f31ee17bd90.png)\n\n**Method 2**\n\nWe can find the distance between the two points by finding the distance of each point from the $y$-axis and then adding.\n\n![](images/f3/f3811804824e802c4cb20af85bac7f21f6c4e0f60e0430607c876e1cf27b7cd3.png)\n\nThe point $(-2,2)$ is at a distance of $2$ from the $y$-axis, and the point $(3,2)$ is at a distance of $3$ from the $y$-axis. Therefore, the distance between the two points is $2+3=5.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186531559 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096678 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1ff8566a-bc65-50a8-bd72-354631883152" :knowledge-point/title "Subtracting a Negative Number"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ce53447-7833-5af3-8f32-25e4bb25afb1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "49.2\\,\\text{ft}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530963} {:answer/id #uuid "94e4a985-0800-55dd-82be-d6e16717c046" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "52.1\\,\\text{ft}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531184} {:answer/id #uuid "984a41f7-7d0c-5d85-9a6b-bd545d610281" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "58.6\\,\\text{ft}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531191} {:answer/id #uuid "b01773cb-7e4c-5838-b4ba-57ccad0bdecd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "62.4\\,\\text{ft}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531243} {:answer/id #uuid "dc6f0ca0-3f27-5c0d-a4ac-1e91b6462a1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "60.3\\,\\text{ft}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531316}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b01773cb-7e4c-5838-b4ba-57ccad0bdecd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "62.4\\,\\text{ft}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531243} :answer-field/id #uuid "efa5e756-b09f-5eba-be5d-3837c1691e2d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531547}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0f0c1499-18ff-5c0e-854a-a4a1f5ed7366" :question/math-academy-id "q-68484" :question/problem "The city of Mexicali, in Mexico, is $6.6$ feet below sea level, while the city of Porto Alegre, in Brazil, is $55.8$ feet above sea level. What is the difference between the elevations of both cities?" :question/worked-solution "To calculate the difference between the elevations of both cities, we must calculate the difference between the city with the highest elevation and the city with the lowest elevation. That is, we must calculate $55.8-(-6.6).$ This gives\n\n$$\n55.8-(-6.6)=55.8+6.6=62.4\\,\\text{ft}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186531582 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110777 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c81cf5ed-8dd7-5174-b8e9-faf63bf0a278" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Quadrilateral"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "58145878-10ab-57b3-b664-f6d36bca4d69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$Q$ and $R$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531059} {:answer/id #uuid "aa794fee-92cb-5205-bbb7-3265b7d85083" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$P$ and $R$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531232} {:answer/id #uuid "b0c121de-66bb-58ae-a63e-bbf43d0fe360" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$P,$ $Q,$ and $R$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531244} {:answer/id #uuid "b5636201-42e6-5b02-b154-839b34a298f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$P$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531251} {:answer/id #uuid "f1f6f0ac-04f0-51ca-89d5-280f541bf412" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$P$ and $Q$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531358}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b0c121de-66bb-58ae-a63e-bbf43d0fe360" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$P,$ $Q,$ and $R$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531244} :answer-field/id #uuid "b42fb396-a4b8-5570-82e5-99d092314e89" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531507}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3ba51678-bfa5-5eea-a51d-29e6a8b3feb3" :question/math-academy-id "q-74587" :question/problem "![](images/9a/9a1f9f1877ae0ecbc37464c5b8b20821070e7927e59dea8d930ceb8f37313722.png)\n\nWhich of the figures above is a parallelogram?" :question/worked-solution "First, recall the hierarchy diagram of quadrilaterals, where each shape below another is a specific type of the one above it.\n\n![](images/1d/1dbe4c3e8ea97c0ac077c37143802366c5817d86965ab1dbc5abf54cd01d27c3.png)\n\nRemember that a parallelogram is a quadrilateral with $2$ pairs of parallel sides.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each shape in turn.\n\n- The shape $P$ is a parallelogram since it has $2$ pairs of parallel sides.\n\n- The shape $Q$ is a square. Therefore, its opposite sides are parallel, so it is a parallelogram.\n\n- The shape $R$ is a rhombus. Since the opposite sides of a rhombus are parallel, it is a parallelogram.\n\n- The shape $S$ is a kite. It has no pairs of opposite sides that are parallel, therefore, it is not a parallelogram.\n\nTherefore, shapes $P,$ $Q,$ and $R$ are parallelograms. The shape $S$ is not parallelogram."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186531631 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147594 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "163d387b-3fd7-5f95-8245-5fb0184b371b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Part of a Number Given a Whole and a Decimal Percentage"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2283e2bc-ebee-5c4d-a9ca-30fbe755b358" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2,125$ liters" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530939} {:answer/id #uuid "3ed97be4-c5cb-5b26-8151-563b09ffe246" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2,225$ liters" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530997} {:answer/id #uuid "4140294a-4de5-516e-a556-10df8fbe6d5d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$3,250$ liters" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531002} {:answer/id #uuid "4fb0f9be-d361-51b6-99a5-14990f65e490" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$3,125$ liters" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531037} {:answer/id #uuid "daa496f1-eb97-5c4e-bcee-4319394a7cda" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2,250$ liters" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531313}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2283e2bc-ebee-5c4d-a9ca-30fbe755b358" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2,125$ liters" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530939} :answer-field/id #uuid "3f118c52-0f0a-5860-a202-cec610c20ffc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531440}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "aeb2c9f4-4f11-5f7d-ac23-e92ca6ecec4e" :question/math-academy-id "q-93027" :question/problem "A water tank with a capacity of $5,000$ liters is filled with water to $42.5%$ of its capacity. How much water is in the tank?" :question/worked-solution "To solve this problem, we can use the formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{part}=\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole}\n$$\n\nIn our case, the whole is the capacity of the tank, which is $5,000$ liters. The percentage is $42.5%,$ and the part is the amount of water in the tank.\n\n**Method 1**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n42.5%=42.5÷100=0.425\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =42.5%\\times 5,000 \\\\  & =0.425\\times 5,000 \\\\  & =2,125\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $42.5%$ of $5,000$ is $2,125.$ Thus, there are $2,125$ liters of water in the tank.\n\n**Method 2**\n\nFirst, we convert the percentage to a fraction:\n\n$$\n42.5%=\\frac{42.5}{100}\n$$\n\nApplying our formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{part} & =\\text{percentage}\\times \\text{whole} \\\\  & =42.5%\\times 5,000 \\\\  & =\\frac{42.5}{100}\\times 5,000 \\\\  & =42.5\\times \\frac{5,000}{100} \\\\  & =42.5\\times 50 \\\\  & =2,125\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $42.5%$ of $5,000$ is $2,125.$ Thus, there are $2,125$ liters of water in the tank."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186531609 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152126 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f7063140-eebe-598c-b530-3c13509d359b" :knowledge-point/title "Classifying Numbers as Rational"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "084d112e-cbf2-52ab-b33c-db2db8f2e5ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530877} {:answer/id #uuid "2abe6b53-714b-5245-80a1-464fc9aa0c47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530958} {:answer/id #uuid "402e9e87-2133-5ebc-b18b-4e9761d1f95c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531000} {:answer/id #uuid "552f6c3a-fd7a-5147-8d6f-0662a6575f22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531051} {:answer/id #uuid "da8778ba-6909-57e5-92c4-9e2a50d98555" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531312}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2abe6b53-714b-5245-80a1-464fc9aa0c47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530958} :answer-field/id #uuid "06e90bf6-f6d2-5efd-a5e4-806286d273e2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531388}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "76ebc4d7-7b51-5dea-a66f-038cad1e5104" :question/math-academy-id "q-98377" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $-\\frac{3}{4}$ is a rational number\n\nII. $\\frac{3}{4}$ is a rational number\n\nIII. $5$ is a rational number" :question/worked-solution "A rational number is any number that can be written as the ratio of two integers.\n\nNow, let's go through each number in turn.\n\n- $-\\frac{3}{4}$ is a rational number. It can be written as $\\frac{(-3)}{4}.$\n\n- $\\frac{3}{4}$ is a rational number.\n\n- $5$ is a rational number. It can be written as $\\frac{5}{1}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186531562 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064231 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c76b2b1b-7536-5b3c-a4c4-6f5e5b72e6ec" :knowledge-point/title "Dividing a Number by Zero"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19ce4107-1ed7-5e21-b139-8243c56f3dcc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530913} {:answer/id #uuid "2ae70c1b-bb34-54d8-98e9-b6aaecd29cb4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "105" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530959} {:answer/id #uuid "4963e121-7b1b-53d9-adda-8c74a2647773" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Undefined" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531021} {:answer/id #uuid "889aa5b5-5e01-5d11-a1cc-344ba1532577" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531163} {:answer/id #uuid "f0a580e5-21fb-52a7-99e6-39faf97f54a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-105" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531354}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4963e121-7b1b-53d9-adda-8c74a2647773" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Undefined" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531021} :answer-field/id #uuid "520d0eb5-427a-54ef-b756-81bb08b44c87" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531447}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "17babc52-289e-5d9d-bc9c-baaf511d4b6f" :question/math-academy-id "q-99756" :question/problem "Find the value of $105÷0.$" :question/worked-solution "We cannot divide any number by zero. Therefore, $105÷0$ is undefined."}]}
